Ticket **#4471** was marked known as a single month/day parser bug. The export’s own
cause logic shows **two** problems were merged into that ticket. File one engineering
ticket per cause; do not keep them under one fix.

<Callout>
Not one issue. Two causes share #4471 because triage matched on subject alone
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
</Callout>

## Causes in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What each cause is

**`parser`** — The shared date parser always reads month first. Day-first tenants
(app, email, and booking-v2 forms) send day-first values; the stored date flips.

**`hint`** — booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the field. Day-first tenants type
month first to match the hint; the form still parses the tenant’s day-first way. Wrong
day, different bug, different fix.

## Tickets

Open one public ticket per cause (report counts come from the table above, recomputed
from the export whenever this page renders):

- parser → GitHub issue titled for the shared month-first parser
- hint → GitHub issue titled for the booking-v3 hint mismatch

